### What to Prepare Locally (Do This First)

Even though you'll skip the VPS for testing, prepare these scripts so they're ready for Launch Day:

#### `scripts/provision-vps.sh`
```bash
#!/bin/bash
# Run as root on Hostinger Ubuntu 24.04 LTS

# 1. Update system
apt update && apt upgrade -y

# 2. Create non-root deploy user
adduser yoka --gecos "" --disabled-password
usermod -aG sudo yoka
mkdir -p /home/yoka/.ssh
cp ~/.ssh/authorized_keys /home/yoka/.ssh/
chown -R yoka:yoka /home/yoka/.ssh

# 3. Harden SSH
sed -i 's/#PermitRootLogin yes/PermitRootLogin no/' /etc/ssh/sshd_config
sed -i 's/#PasswordAuthentication yes/PasswordAuthentication no/' /etc/ssh/sshd_config
systemctl restart sshd

# 4. UFW Firewall
ufw default deny incoming
ufw default allow outgoing
ufw allow 22/tcp
ufw allow 80/tcp
ufw allow 443/tcp
ufw --force enable

# 5. Node.js 20 LTS
curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_20.x | bash -
apt-get install -y nodejs
npm install -g pm2 pnpm typescript

# 6. MySQL 8.0
apt install -y mysql-server
mysql_secure_installation
# Configure my.cnf (see below)

# 7. Redis 7.2
apt install -y redis-server
# Configure redis.conf (see below)

# 8. Nginx
apt install -y nginx
systemctl enable nginx
```

#### MySQL `my.cnf` Tuning (for 8GB VPS)
```ini
[mysqld]
innodb_buffer_pool_size        = 4G
innodb_buffer_pool_instances   = 4
innodb_log_file_size           = 512M
innodb_flush_log_at_trx_commit = 2
max_connections                = 300
slow_query_log                 = 1
long_query_time                = 2
default_time_zone              = '+03:00'
character-set-server           = utf8mb4
collation-server               = utf8mb4_unicode_ci
```

#### Redis `redis.conf` Tuning
```
requirepass YokaRedis2026!Strong
maxmemory 1gb
maxmemory-policy volatile-lru
bind 127.0.0.1
protected-mode yes
```

**✅ Acceptance Criteria (Production):** `systemctl status mysql redis-server nginx` → all `active (running)`

